  "content": {
    "text": "00:00 Speaker A\nSpaceX, day two. Um, because the shares, I believe last I checked, they were indicated to to open higher. Um, after rising on Friday. And like you and I were\n00:14 Speaker A\nSpaceX'd out maybe.\n00:15 Speaker B\nSure.\n00:15 Speaker A\nUm, after talking about it so much that day. But like at at the end of the day, the process itself was uneventful, right? Which is good.\n00:26 Speaker B\nMhm.\n00:27 Speaker A\nYeah. Good from the Nasdaq's perspective, good from the underwriters' perspective, good from the SpaceX's perspective. Like nothing dramatic went wrong. The stock went up a reasona-- it opened at a reasonable place, it went up a reasonable amount. It wasn't like, nothing about it was crazy.\n00:43 Speaker A\nSo,\n00:44 Speaker B\nI've seems like a win. I think we're already at the point where I care but don't care about what the price is doing. Well, because sort of my argument's been people keep asking about it getting in the indexes, which it won't be in the S&P 500 presumably unless the rules now change, even though they said they weren't going to change them. It won't be in the S&P for a year. Um, it will be in the Q's I think by mid-July, the QQQ, uh, the Nasdaq 100 ETF. But\n1:13 Speaker B\nit won't have that big of a weighting. I just don't think a company that trades at 100 times sales is going to tell us much more about the market and the market environment other than just investor sentiment, a little bit of euphoria, the same way that when we're looking at a heat map, we look at Tesla. And it's okay, everything that is a little bit on the junkier side from a profitability standpoint and has a very high valuation is up today. SpaceX will go in that bucket.\n1:46 Speaker B\nBut I think that's where SpaceX just stays for me now. I think getting the 20% pop told me that, okay, the market would be ready to accept Anthropic or Open AI.\n1:58 Speaker A\nMhm.\n1:59 Speaker B\nBut beyond that, beyond the market probably won't sell off those stocks on the first day, those are totally different stories than SpaceX. How SpaceX trades over the next two to three weeks, a couple months, I don't think tells me how Anthropic will do as a stock. So I'm sort of like, all right, here we are. SPCX, I'll look at it every now and then.\n2:15 Speaker A\nIt's not really about the first month or year or whatever. It's about the life of the company. And you pointed out Facebook when it went public, of course, had a very rocky opening and then it took, I mean, Tesla for that matter. Like it took a while for Tesla to be Tesla from a stock perspective. And so, like, and SpaceX is especially a company again, where it's like, it's not about what it's going to be making this year or next year. It's sort of these long-term, lofty goals that that it has set for itself. So,\n2:53 Speaker A\nyou know, we can kind of like put it to the side for the moment.\n2:56 Speaker B\nYeah, and I think what you keep an eye on is how those long-term lofty goals shift over time.",
    "text_blocks": [
      "00:00 Speaker A",
      "SpaceX, day two. Um, because the shares, I believe last I checked, they were indicated to to open higher. Um, after rising on Friday. And like you and I were",
      "00:14 Speaker A",
      "SpaceX'd out maybe.",
      "00:15 Speaker B",
      "Sure.",
      "00:15 Speaker A",
      "Um, after talking about it so much that day. But like at at the end of the day, the process itself was uneventful, right? Which is good.",
      "00:26 Speaker B",
      "Mhm.",
      "00:27 Speaker A",
      "Yeah. Good from the Nasdaq's perspective, good from the underwriters' perspective, good from the SpaceX's perspective. Like nothing dramatic went wrong. The stock went up a reasona-- it opened at a reasonable place, it went up a reasonable amount. It wasn't like, nothing about it was crazy.",
      "00:43 Speaker A",
      "So,",
      "00:44 Speaker B",
      "I've seems like a win. I think we're already at the point where I care but don't care about what the price is doing. Well, because sort of my argument's been people keep asking about it getting in the indexes, which it won't be in the S&P 500 presumably unless the rules now change, even though they said they weren't going to change them. It won't be in the S&P for a year. Um, it will be in the Q's I think by mid-July, the QQQ, uh, the Nasdaq 100 ETF. But",
      "1:13 Speaker B",
      "it won't have that big of a weighting. I just don't think a company that trades at 100 times sales is going to tell us much more about the market and the market environment other than just investor sentiment, a little bit of euphoria, the same way that when we're looking at a heat map, we look at Tesla. And it's okay, everything that is a little bit on the junkier side from a profitability standpoint and has a very high valuation is up today. SpaceX will go in that bucket.",
      "1:46 Speaker B",
      "But I think that's where SpaceX just stays for me now. I think getting the 20% pop told me that, okay, the market would be ready to accept Anthropic or Open AI.",
      "1:58 Speaker A",
      "Mhm.",
      "1:59 Speaker B",
      "But beyond that, beyond the market probably won't sell off those stocks on the first day, those are totally different stories than SpaceX. How SpaceX trades over the next two to three weeks, a couple months, I don't think tells me how Anthropic will do as a stock. So I'm sort of like, all right, here we are. SPCX, I'll look at it every now and then.",
      "2:15 Speaker A",
      "It's not really about the first month or year or whatever. It's about the life of the company. And you pointed out Facebook when it went public, of course, had a very rocky opening and then it took, I mean, Tesla for that matter. Like it took a while for Tesla to be Tesla from a stock perspective. And so, like, and SpaceX is especially a company again, where it's like, it's not about what it's going to be making this year or next year. It's sort of these long-term, lofty goals that that it has set for itself. So,",
      "2:53 Speaker A",
      "you know, we can kind of like put it to the side for the moment.",
